  description:
  - As years go by, Truffle Hogs have begun to lose the herd mentality that was present
    in the species prior to the Mist's presence. Immature specimens still display
    remnants of this behavior, and will follow closely to their parent until reaching
    maturity.
  - Unaltered forms of the Truffle Hog still exist today and are used in searching
    for various mushrooms and roots, as well as for their high meat yield. Such specimens
    are often hard to come by in the wild, and their preservation relies on selective
    breeding and reduced mist exposure.
  leftText: 
  rightText: As years go by, Truffle Hogs have begun to lose the herd mentality that
    was present in the species prior to the Mist's presence. Immature specimens still
    display remnants of this behavior, and will follow closely to their parent until
    reaching maturity. Unaltered forms of the Truffle Hog still exist today and are
    used in scouting for various mushrooms and roots, as well as for their high meat
    yield. Such specimens are hard to come by in the wild, and their preservation
    relies on selective breeding and reduced mist exposure.
